# What the deploy does NOT need to upload.
#
# `vercel deploy` tars the working directory and sends it. Unfiltered that is ~600 MB here and the
# upload simply aborts — which is how this file came to exist.
#
# WHAT IS EXCLUDED AND WHY EACH ONE IS SAFE:
#
#   reference/     366 MB of upstream clones — the Uniswap interface, the sponsor's privacy
#                  monorepo, the hackathon repo. Read by humans and by research, never by the
#                  build. This is the whole reason the upload was failing.
#   node_modules/  221 MB, reinstalled remotely from the lockfile.
#   _bmad*/        planning artifacts and the workflow engine. Not build inputs.
#   .relayer/      the relayer's file-backed stores. Local state, and some of it is a funded
#                  signer's business — it must never leave this machine.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED:
#
#   vendor/        the privacy SDK installs from here (`file:vendor/…` in the lockfile), so an
#                  install without it fails outright. 180 KB.
#   docs/          one small reviewer-facing page (architecture.md). Nothing in the build reads
#                  it, and it costs nothing to keep the upload identical to the repo.
#   evidence/      small, and it is the project's record of what it has actually done on mainnet.
#   apps/web/dist/ THE ARTIFACT ITSELF. It is uploaded rather than built remotely — see the note
#                  in vercel.json. Excluding it would deploy an empty site.
#
reference/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
_bmad/
_bmad-output/
.relayer/
.secrets/
.agents/
.thoughts/
.git/
.vercel/
**/.vercel/
contracts/target/
contracts/.snfoundry_cache/
context/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The site builds on Vercel from source; nothing generated locally under it should ride along.
apps/site/.next
**/.next/
apps/site/.source
apps/site/.env.local
apps/site/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
